# mp-754090 (Li4Fe2TeWO12) Fe-sublattice spin model, v3 (2026-09-21): identical to v2 except that
# J is mapped from the TIGHT same-cell FM/AFM pair (data/dft_staging_tight/mp-754090/{afm_1_afm,
# fm_in_1_afm}: both orderings relaxed with ISIF=2 in the same relaxed cell, EDIFF=1e-6 eV,
# EDIFFG=-0.01 eV/A) instead of the loose MPRelaxSet pair (FM and AFM each at its own ISIF=3 optimum).
# A Heisenberg J is defined at a fixed lattice, so the same-cell pair is the consistent mapping:
#   dE = E_AFM - E_FM = 44.53729 meV/cell (loose pair: 48.23354), J = dE/8 = 5.5672 meV (loose: 6.0292),
# i.e. an 8% protocol spread that the paper quotes as the systematic uncertainty of J.
# D = 0.193 meV per bond is unchanged (separate constrained noncollinear calculation).
#
# ---- v2 header (bond-counting correction, ordered start, still valid) ----
#
# What changed vs in.mp754090_effective.lammps / in.mp754090_dynamics.lammps and why:
#
# 1. Exchange constant halved: J = 6.029 meV, not 12.058 meV.
#    LAMMPS spin/exchange (pair_spin_exchange.cpp, full neighbour list, 0.5 factor per visit)
#    evaluates E_ex = -sum_{bonds} J(r) s_i.s_j with every bond counted ONCE. Flipping the Fe0
#    sublattice (the DFT AFM configuration) reverses the 4 inter-sublattice bonds per 2-Fe cell,
#    so E_AFM - E_FM = 2 * 4 * J = 8 J. With the DFT value dE = 48.23354 meV/cell this gives
#    J = 6.029 meV. The earlier file used dE / 4 = 12.058 meV, i.e. a model whose FM-AFM energy
#    difference is 96.5 meV/cell -- twice the DFT number (verified numerically with `run 0` on
#    the old input: E_AFM - E_FM = 96.46 meV/cell). Every temperature scale of the old sweep is
#    therefore ~2x too high.
# 2. The 5.25 A cutoff also captures 2 same-sublattice Fe-Fe bonds per Fe (5.127 A, lattice
#    translations), which the FM/AFM pair cannot resolve (they are unchanged by the flip). They
#    are kept with the same J -- an explicit assumption J_intra = J_inter, stated in the paper --
#    because no cutoff can separate 5.127 A from the 5.112-5.157 A inter-sublattice shell.
# 3. Ordered (FM, +z) initial state instead of a random start relaxed with spin/lbfgs: the old
#    protocol left a multi-domain state with |m| = 0.20 already at T = 0, so the sweep's absolute
#    scale meant nothing. Starting from the ground state and thermalising with Langevin dynamics
#    gives an |m|(T) whose scale is physical (|m| -> 1 as T -> 0).
# 4. 4 ps per temperature (2x longer), |m| averaged over the second half, 3 seeds per T.
#
# D = 0.193 meV along y, per bond, unchanged (per-bond convention of the DFT extraction matches
# spin/dmi, which also counts each bond once). Anisotropy still 0 (unknown, not guessed).
# spin/magelec with zero strength stays as the documented hybrid/overlay segfault workaround.

units           metal
atom_style      spin
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map array

read_data       mp754090_fe.data
replicate       16 8 8

set             group all spin 4.15 0.0 0.0 1.0     # FM ground state along +z (mu_s = 4.15 mu_B)

variable        j_eff_eV equal 0.0055671613          # = 0.04453729 eV / 8 (tight pair)
variable        d_shell equal 5.132075
variable        exch_a equal v_j_eff_eV*2.718281828/4.0
variable        rc_exch equal 5.25
variable        d_eV equal 0.00019324
variable        rc_dmi equal 5.25

pair_style      hybrid/overlay spin/exchange ${rc_exch} spin/dmi ${rc_dmi} spin/magelec ${rc_exch}
pair_coeff      * * spin/exchange exchange ${rc_exch} ${exch_a} 0.0 ${d_shell} offset yes
pair_coeff      * * spin/dmi dmi ${rc_dmi} ${d_eV} 0.0 1.0 0.0
pair_coeff      * * spin/magelec magelec ${rc_exch} 0.0 1.0 1.0 1.0   # zero strength: segfault workaround only

neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 check yes delay 20

fix             1 all precession/spin zeeman 0.0 0.0 0.0 1.0
fix_modify      1 energy yes
# alpha (Langevin damping) defaults to 1.0 for the equilibrium |m|(T) sweep: |m|(T) at equilibrium does not
# depend on alpha, but the thermalisation time of the softest magnons scales as 1/alpha and at 0.05 the
# 20 ps runs were still drifting at the temperatures nearest the transition (window-drift check in the
# analysis). Override with -var alpha 0.05 to reproduce the earlier runs.
variable        alpha index 1.0
fix             2 all langevin/spin ${runtemp} ${alpha} ${runseed}
fix             3 all nve/spin lattice frozen

timestep        0.0001

compute         out_mag all spin
thermo_style    custom step time pe c_out_mag[4] c_out_mag[5]
thermo          100

# nsteps defaults to 200000 (20 ps): the 4 ps sweep (logs_v3_4ps) was still drifting downward at
# 100-175 K across its averaged half (|m| 0.52 -> 0.36 at 100 K), so 20 ps, last 10 ps averaged.
variable        nsteps index 200000
run             ${nsteps}
print           "DYNAMICS_T${runtemp}_DONE"
